*THE FOLLOWING IS A SHORT SAMPLE PROBLEM. EXTENSIVE TEST PROBLEMS CAN         01
*BE PREPARED BY MODIFICATION OF EXISTING 709 OR 7090 ROUTINES IN              02
*ACCORDANCE WITH THE INSTRUCTIONS IN THE WRITE-UP.                            03
*  CONVERSION OF BCD TO BINARY USING A CONVERT INSTRUCTION.                   04
*  THE BCD NUMBER IS 32767 WHICH WILL BECOME OCTAL 77777 UPON                 05
* CONVERSION.  THE COMPUTER WILL HALT WITH THIS RESULT IN THE AC.             06
*  PRESSING THE START BUTTON WILL REPEAT THE TEST.  OTHER BCD NUMBERS         07
*  MAY BE USED IN THE TEST BY CHANGING THE CONTENTS OF THE LOCATION           08
*  LABELLED BCDWD.                                                            09
       LDQ     *+3                                                            10
       STQ     2             INITIALIZE SIMULATOR.                            11
       TRA     *+2                                                            12
       TRA     S709                                                           13
       LDQ     BCDWD         LOAD BCD WORD                                    14
       PXD     ,0                 CLEAR AC                                    15
       PZE     T,,1*16+6     SIMULATE CAQ T,,6                                16
       ARS     16                 PUSH OFF ADDRESS SUM                        17
       HPR                        HALT WITH RESULT IN BINARY IN AC            18
       TRA     *-5                PRESSING START REPEATS TEST                 19
 BCDWD BCI     1,032767                                                       20
*LOCATION OF T MUST BE LESS THAN OCTAL 31426.                                 21
 T     DUP     1,10                                                           22
       VFD     20/**100000-T*100000,16/T+10                                   23
       DUP     1,10                                                           24
       VFD     20/**10000-100000-T*10000,16/T+20                              25
       DUP     1,10                                                           26
       VFD     20/**1000-20000-T*1000,16/T+30                                 27
       DUP     1,10                                                           28
       VFD     20/**100-3000-T*100,16/T+40                                    29
       DUP     1,10                                                           30
       VFD     20/**10-400-T*10,16/T+50                                       31
       DUP     1,10                                                           32
       VFD     20/*-50-T,16/0                                                 33
 S709  EQU     32000     USE THIS IF SIMULATOR IS ABSOLUTE AT 320000.         34
       END                                                                    35
